{"questions":[{"question_id":"1lg0z8c3v","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2007 Paper 1 Offline","year":2007,"examDate":2007,"subject":"physics","chapter":"electrostatics","chapterGroup":"electricity","topic":"electric-flux-and-gauss-law","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"pconsider-a-neutral-conducting-sphere-a-positive-point-ch-jee-advanced-physics-motion-qxuuprqli79qdhab","content":"<p>Consider a neutral conducting sphere. A positive point charge is placed outside the sphere. The net charge on the sphere is then,</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"negative and distributed uniformly over the surface of the sphere"},{"identifier":"B","content":"negative and appears only at the point on the sphere closest to the point charge"},{"identifier":"C","content":"negative and distributed non-uniformly over the entire surface of the sphere"},{"identifier":"D","content":"zero"}],"correct_options":["D"],"explanation":"<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1mggcqz3s/ac403717-2370-4a9d-b54f-a9ae8540b68b/43c1cb80-a35f-11f0-b814-0f72f73fa4cf/file-jaoe38c1mggcqz3t.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/jaoe38c1mggcqz3s/ac403717-2370-4a9d-b54f-a9ae8540b68b/43c1cb80-a35f-11f0-b814-0f72f73fa4cf/file-jaoe38c1mggcqz3t.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;max-height:40vh;vertical-align:baseline\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2007 Paper 1 Offline Physics - Electrostatics Question 22 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/jaoe38c1mggcqz3s/ac403717-2370-4a9d-b54f-a9ae8540b68b/43c1cb80-a35f-11f0-b814-0f72f73fa4cf/file-jaoe38c1mggcqz3t.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/jaoe38c1mggcqz3s/ac403717-2370-4a9d-b54f-a9ae8540b68b/43c1cb80-a35f-11f0-b814-0f72f73fa4cf/file-jaoe38c1mggcqz3t.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1mggcqz3s/ac403717-2370-4a9d-b54f-a9ae8540